{"reply": "Thanks, Heather. Yes, there is one open recall on your car. It's NM-24R01, "Rear camera image may not display". The fix is a software update that takes about 45 minutes, and the parts are available. This recall repair is done at no cost to you.

The brake pads aren't part of that recall, so they would be a separate job and I can't say they'd be free. Your basic warranty is past its limits, and it lists brake pads as excluded. If you'd like a person to look at the brakes, I can pass that on.

Which branch would you like for the recall work?", "action": "answered", "escalation_reason": "none", "summary": "", "policy_rules_cited": ["P-01", "P-03", "P-04"]}
